# A fed fox among a flock raises a kit once it is two days old, and then waits
# LITTER_GAP days for the next: about one kit in its ~9-day life, so foxes
# grow no faster than the flock can feed them (at a kit every 5 days they
# boomed and ate the flock out within a month: tuning/foxes-hunt-more).
seed 5
outside soil
map {
  gggggggggggggggggggggggggggg
  ggCgggCgggCgggCgggCgggCggggg
  gggggggggggggggggggggggggggg
  ggggCg~~~~~~~~~~~~ggCggggggg
  gggggg~~~~~~~~~~~~gggggggggg
  ggCggg~~~~~~~~~~~~gggCgggggg
  gggggg~~~~~~~~~~~~gggggggggg
  ggggCg~~~~~~~~~~~~ggCggggggg
  gggggggggggggggggggggggggggg
  ggCgggCgggCgggCgggCgggCggggg
  ggggggggggggFggggggggggggggg
  ggCgggCgggCgggCgggCgggCggggg
  gggggggggggggggggggggggggggg
  gggggggggggggggggggggggggggg
}
legend {
  g grass
  ~ water
  C chicken
  F fox
}

run 84h
expect born fox == 1                       # one kit
expect max last_litter of fox >= 12        # its day (2 or 3) + 10: no other before day 12
